  "narrative": "All estimates are interpreted as already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For direction -1, a positive signed estimate means the exposed group has a more negative dependency score, i.e. stronger CRISPR dependency; for direction +1, a positive signed estimate means the exposed group has a less negative/higher dependency score, i.e. weaker dependency. H41 accepts the KEAP1-loss/weak-NFE2L2 pattern within adenocarcinoma: the signed estimate is +0.793 with interval +0.769 to +0.817. This is several standard deviations on the dependency-score scale and is far larger than the small null associations seen for direct receptor-tyrosine-kinase target hypotheses. H42 accepts the MSI-high/strong-WRN association among TP53-wild-type cells: signed estimate +0.780, interval +0.747 to +0.813. Thus the WRN effect is not confined to TP53-loss backgrounds. H43 and H44 test modification of the accepted USP7 and SMARCA2 effects by ARID1A loss and TP53 loss. Their interaction estimates are small and cross zero: H43 -0.016 with interval -0.066 to +0.034, and H44 -0.015 with interval -0.064 to +0.035. I therefore reject these interaction claims as unsupported, while preserving the already accepted main effects and their prior robustness checks. H45 rejects the EGFR-amplification/EGFR-dependency hypothesis after removing KRAS and BRAF co-alterations: signed estimate +0.010, interval -0.020 to +0.041. H46 rejects the parallel ERBB2 conditional claim: signed estimate -0.011, interval -0.047 to +0.024. H47 rejects the cross-target hypothesis that EGFR amplification in RAS/RAF wild-type cells increases dependence on KRAS: signed estimate -0.0005, interval -0.033 to +0.032. H48 is rejected even though the 95% interval narrowly excludes zero, because the signed estimate is -0.020 for a direction -1 claim, meaning the observed association is weakly opposite to the hypothesis: TP53 loss is associated with a higher/less negative DHX9 score, i.e. weaker dependency. The magnitude is tiny relative to the outcome standard deviation and only marginal in a multiplicity-rich discovery setting, so I do not accept the original directional claim or its reversal as scientifically meaningful. H49, H50, H51, and H53 are all close to null: KIF18A/MSI-high, RIT1/KRAS in BRAF-wild-type cells, RPL11/MYC amplification within high MYC expression, and TMED10/ERBB2 amplification show intervals crossing zero with very small point estimates. I also reassess the original EGFR claim H3 using the overall borderline result plus the KRAS-wild-type and KRAS/BRAF-wild-type conditional null checks. Given that the overall estimate is small, its interval includes zero, and the mechanistically motivated conditional analyses are also null, H3 is rejected and closed as an unsupported dataset association. The strongest currently supported associations remain the very large TP53-wild-type/USP7, SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2, MSI-high/WRN, and KEAP1-loss/weak-NFE2L2 effects, plus the robustness checks in adenocarcinoma and TP53-wild-type subsets for the NFE2L2 and WRN claims. Because H13 is large but directionally counterintuitive, I request independent validation for H13. These remain associations within the supplied dataset, not causal effects or externally generalizable clinical claims.",
  "research_notes": "Updated accepted main associations: H6 TP53 WT stronger USP7 dependency; H7 SMARCA4 loss stronger SMARCA2 dependency, independently validated; H9 MSI-high stronger WRN dependency; H13 KEAP1 loss weaker NFE2L2 dependency/higher dependency score. Additional accepted robustness: H41 NFE2L2 KEAP1 effect in adenocarcinoma; H42 WRN MSI-high effect in TP53 WT; earlier H14/H15 SMARCA4 effect with and without ARID1A loss, H17 WRN higher-TMB comparator, H18 USP7 MYC-amplified, H21 USP7 KY, H22 NFE2L2 KY, H23 SMARCA2 KY, H31 NFE2L2 STK11 WT, H33 WRN adenocarcinoma. Interaction null: H16 no ARID1A modification of SMARCA4/SMARCA2; H25 no KEAP1-by-TP53 interaction; H43 no ARID1A modification of USP7/TP53 effect; H44 no TP53 modification of SMARCA4/SMARCA2 effect. Rejected/null closed: H1 KRAS, H2 BRAF, H3 EGFR after conditional nulls, H4/H46 ERBB2 overall and KRAS/BRAF WT, H5 MDM2/TP53, H8 ARID1A alone, H11 STAT3/PIK3CA, H12 POLR2A/MYC, H19/H45 EGFR conditional, H47 KRAS dependency in EGFR WT context, H48 DHX9/TP53 loss opposite and tiny, H49 KIF18A/MSI, H50 RIT1/KRAS BRAF WT, H51 RPL11/MYC high-expression, H53 TMED10/ERBB2. Pending independent validation request: H13. If H13 validates well, consider validating H9 or H6. Remaining discovery queue should focus on H26, H27, H28, H29, H30, H32, H34, H35, H36, H37, H38, H39, H40, and H52, prioritizing lineage-subtype robustness and any outcome/predictor pairs not yet directly tested. Avoid interpreting small 95%-borderline results like DHX9/TP53 as meaningful without larger effect size or validation.",
