  "narrative": "All new estimates are interpreted as already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For the direction -1 CDKN2A-MDM2 claims, a positive signed estimate means stronger MDM2 dependency in CDKN2A-loss cells. The key new mechanistic results are H165 and H166. H165 estimates the CDKN2A-loss MDM2 difference among TP53-intact cells with copy_number_9p21 <= -0.5: +0.122 (95% CI +0.073 to +0.171). H166 estimates the same CDKN2A-loss MDM2 difference in all cells with copy_number_9p21 <= -0.5: +0.135 (95% CI +0.091 to +0.179). These are valid, precise, and large relative to MDM2 SD (about 0.54 and 0.59 SD), so I accept them as within-dataset associations and keep them active pending validation. They argue against the idea that low 9p21 copy loss alone fully mimics CDKN2A loss, because CDKN2A-loss still associates with stronger MDM2 dependency within low-9p21 cells. However, CDKN2A loss is enriched for low 9p21 and complete separation from copy-number severity may remain imperfect. H174 is a useful MTAP co-deletion control: among TP53-intact CDKN2A-intact low-9p21 cells, MTAP loss is not meaningfully associated with stronger MDM2 dependency (+0.031, CI -0.028 to +0.090), so I reject that MTAP loss alone explains the CDKN2A-MDM2 signal in this stratum. Outcome specificity also holds: CDKN2A loss is not associated with USP7 (+0.002, CI -0.038 to +0.043) or WRN (-0.007, CI -0.034 to +0.021) dependencies, so I reject H167 and H168. H173 shows the CDKN2A-MDM2 association in the TP53-intact MYC-amplified context is positive (+0.131, CI +0.037 to +0.225), but the exposed cell count is small (57), so I accept it only as supportive context and not as a precise effect estimate. Technical robustness continues to support the major accepted effects: lower screen-quality cells still show strong TP53-intact versus TP53-loss USP7 dependency (+0.797, CI +0.764 to +0.830), SMARCA4-loss versus SMARCA4-intact SMARCA2 dependency (+0.774, CI +0.743 to +0.804), and MSI-high versus MSI-stable WRN dependency (+0.781, CI +0.730 to +0.832). These are within-dataset associations and not causal or generalizable claims. Null probes reduce concern about overbroad interpretation: marker D with MDM2 is small and not supporting its registered direction (-0.019, CI -0.039 to +0.001); marker E with STAT3 is tiny (+0.015, CI -0.007 to +0.036); PTEN loss with BRAF dependency is tiny and effectively null (+0.023, CI -0.000 to +0.046). I reject these because they are not scientifically meaningful and intervals include or nearly include zero. Multiplicity is controlled by judgment and consistency rather than a single p-value threshold: the CDKN2A-MDM2 results are consistent with prior CDKN2A-MDM2 discovery and validation, while null probes and outcome-specificity checks do not show generic dependency patterns. Because the central residual issue is whether CDKN2A-MDM2 remains in low 9p21 copy-loss cells, I request independent validation for H166, the unstratified low-9p21 CDKN2A-MDM2 comparison.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 12 appraise. Core CDKN2A-MDM2 mechanism now much stronger: H165 TP53-intact low9p21 CDKN2A loss +0.122 [0.073,0.171]; H166 all low9p21 CDKN2A loss +0.135 [0.091,0.179]; both accepted active. H174 MTAP alone in TP53-intact CDKN2A-intact low9p21 null/reject. H167 CDKN2A-USP7 null/reject and H168 CDKN2A-WRN null/reject, supporting outcome specificity. H173 CDKN2A-MDM2 among TP53-intact MYC-amplified positive +0.131 [0.037,0.225] but small exposed n, accept closed as context. Lower screen quality robustness accepted for TP53-intact-USP7, SMARCA4-loss-SMARCA2, MSI-high-WRN. Null probes rejected: marker D-MDM2, marker E-STAT3, PTEN-BRAF. Validation requested for H166 to test low-9p21 CDKN2A-MDM2 independent split. Next planned proposals: CDKN2A-MDM2 among TP53-intact MTAP-intact low9p21; CDKN2A-MDM2 among deeper low9p21 <= -0.75; MTAP alone among CDKN2A-intact low9p21. Continue interpreting only signed estimates; accept no causal/generalizable claims. Use outcome SD and absolute effect because 10% relative rule is awkward for negative continuous dependency scores.",
