  "narrative": "No assessments are due, and no independent validation can be requested because the validation budget is exhausted. The most valuable next comparisons are focused within-dataset tests that resolve the unexpected research_signature_B PTEN/STAT3 finding while asking whether research_signature_B is a generic modifier of the other strong accepted associations or a PTEN/STAT3-specific context. I registered four PTEN/STAT3 signature-B stratum tests. The extreme-high test (signature_B >= 1) uses direction +1 to test the working hypothesis that PTEN-loss cells show attenuation or reversal of the accepted stronger STAT3 dependency in that stratum: a positive signed mean estimate would mean PTEN-loss cells have less negative, or weaker, STAT3 dependency than PTEN-intact cells. The middle-band test (-0.5 <= signature_B <= 0.5) and extreme-low test (signature_B <= -1) use direction -1 so that a positive signed estimate means the accepted PTEN-loss/stronger-STAT3-dependency pattern is preserved: PTEN-loss cells have more negative STAT3 dependency than PTEN-intact cells. The extreme-high interaction also uses direction +1; a positive signed interaction would mean that the PTEN-loss effect in signature_B >= 1 is more positive, hence attenuated or reversed, relative to the complement, whereas a negative signed interaction would mean it is stronger in that extreme-high stratum. I also registered signature_B interaction controls for the other principal accepted associations: SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2, TP53-status/USP7, KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2, MSI-high/WRN, and CDKN2A-loss/MDM2. These interaction directions are chosen to align with the accepted raw contrasts for those effects, so for a near-zero interaction there is little evidence of signature-B modification. For direction -1 accepted-effect controls, a positive signed interaction would mean the accepted effect is stronger in high signature_B than in its complement, whereas a negative signed interaction would mean attenuation in high signature_B. For KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2, the accepted raw contrast is positive because KEAP1-loss cells have weaker NFE2L2 dependency, so direction +1 aligns with the accepted effect. These tests distinguish several alternatives: if only PTEN/STAT3 changes across signature_B, signature_B may mark a PTEN/STAT3-specific constructed context or interaction artifact; if several accepted effects are modified, signature_B may be a broad technical or population modifier; if signature_B interactions are near zero and PTEN/STAT3 middle and low strata preserve the accepted effect, the original reversed signature-B interaction is more likely an isolated constructed-signature interaction rather than a general biological effect modifier. All interpretations remain within-dataset associations and are not causal or external-generalizability claims.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 15 attempt 2. No assessments due and no validation budget remains. Registered nine new unresolved comparisons to focus the active H205-H207 research_signature_B PTEN/STAT3 issue. PTEN/STAT3 direct strata: extreme-high signature_B >= 1 with direction +1 to test attenuation/reversal; middle band -0.5 to 0.5 and extreme-low <= -1 with direction -1 to test preservation of accepted PTEN-loss stronger STAT3 dependency; extreme-high >=1 interaction with direction +1 to test attenuation/reversal relative to complement. Added signature_B interaction controls for other accepted effects: SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2, TP53-status/USP7, KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2, MSI-high/WRN, and CDKN2A-loss/MDM2. These controls test whether signature_B is a generic modifier or isolated to PTEN/STAT3. All proposals are new comparisons with no parent to avoid refinement-evidence errors. Main accepted associations remain within-dataset: TP53 non-loss stronger USP7, SMARCA4 loss stronger SMARCA2, MSI-high stronger WRN, KEAP1 loss weaker NFE2L2, PTEN loss stronger STAT3, CDKN2A loss stronger MDM2, especially in low-9p21 contexts. No causal or generalizability claims are made."
