  "narrative": "No validation was requested because the voluntary validation budget is exhausted. All estimates are already signed to the registered claim direction. For direction -1 mean contrasts, positive signed estimates mean the exposed group has more negative dependency scores, i.e. stronger dependency; for direction -1 interactions, positive signed estimates mean the exposed-comparator effect is stronger in the named subgroup than in its complement. For direction +1 contrasts, a positive signed estimate means the raw exposed-minus-comparator contrast is positive, i.e. higher/less negative dependency scores for the exposed group, or a more positive raw interaction for direction +1 interactions.\n\nThe PTEN-loss/STAT3-dependency pattern is now much clearer. The accepted overall PTEN-loss effect is preserved in cells with research_signature_b <= 0.5: H207 (<=0.5) gives +0.392 [0.327, 0.457], H209 (-0.5 to 0.5) gives +0.367 [0.278, 0.456], and H210 (<= -1) gives +0.387 [0.256, 0.517]. These are roughly 1.5-1.6 STAT3 SD and intervals exclude zero, so I accept them. In high research_signature_b, direct mean differences are not statistically meaningful: H206 (>=0.5) gives +0.018 [-0.025, 0.061] and H208 (>=1) gives +0.021 [-0.041, 0.083]. Because direction is +1, these positive point estimates would correspond to weaker STAT3 dependency in PTEN-loss cells, but their magnitudes are tiny (<0.1 STAT3 SD) and intervals cross zero. I therefore reject H206 and H208 as claims of a meaningful positive direct high-signature-B difference. They are, however, consistent with an attenuated or nearly absent PTEN effect in high signature B rather than a strong reversal.\n\nThe interaction results support that context dependence. H211, pre-registered specifically for the extreme-high stratum research_signature_b >= 1, gives +0.338 [0.254, 0.422] (about 1.4 STAT3 SD), indicating that the raw PTEN-loss effect in high signature B is much more positive, hence attenuated or absent, relative to the complement. I accept H211 and close it. H205 is the broader high-signature-B interaction (>=0.5), +0.411 [0.333, 0.488]. It was originally registered post hoc after H203 gave the opposite direction, but the new pre-registered H211 and the direct stratum results strongly corroborate the same interpretation: PTEN-loss strengthens STAT3 dependency in lower signature-B strata but this association is attenuated toward zero in high signature B. I therefore accept H205 as a within-dataset context association, while keeping it active because research_signature_b is an artificial constructed assay and no independent validation remains.\n\nThe control interactions test whether research_signature_b is a generic modifier. H212 (SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2) is near null (+0.025 [-0.016, 0.067]); H214 (KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2) is near null (+0.026 [-0.015, 0.068]); H215 (MSI-high/WRN) is essentially null (-0.006 [-0.068, 0.055]). I reject the registered positive modification claims for H212, H214, and H215. H213 (TP53-status/USP7) shows a statistically supported opposite-signed result: signed estimate -0.058 [-0.102, -0.014]. Under direction -1, this means the accepted USP7 effect is modestly attenuated in high signature B relative to its complement. However, the magnitude is only about 0.16 USP7 SD and it is an opposite-signed result among multiple controls; I do not promote it as a meaningful context effect and reject H213 as registered. Overall, research_signature_b is not a generic modifier of the accepted dependency associations, but it is selectively associated with modification of PTEN/STAT3 and CDKN2A/MDM2 in this dataset.\n\nThe strongest new effect-modification result is H216: CDKN2A-loss/MDM2 interaction in high research_signature_b gives +0.195 [0.116, 0.274]. Under direction -1, this means the CDKN2A-loss effect is much stronger in cells with research_signature_b >= 0.5 than in its complement. The interval excludes zero and the interaction is about 0.86 MDM2 SD, which is scientifically meaningful relative to the MDM2 outcome distribution. Because the exposure and subgroup are both pre-registered and the result is strong, I accept H216 as a within-dataset association. I keep it active because research_signature_b is an arbitrary constructed signature, the effect could be a synthetic-context artifact, and direct high/low stratum and confounder-stratified analyses are needed to estimate raw effect sizes and check dependence on TP53 status, MTAP/9p21 co-deletion contexts, or other correlated variables. No validation budget remains, so acceptance here is explicitly a discovery-stage within-dataset conclusion, not a causal or generalizable claim.\n\nThe proposed follow-ups are therefore focused on H216 and the PTEN/STAT3 signature-B context: direct CDKN2A-MDM2 estimates in high and low signature B, an extreme-high signature-B interaction, and high-signature-B estimates restricted to TP53-intact or low-9p21 contexts to see whether the modification survives in known mechanistic strata. Marker-D interaction controls for CDKN2A/MDM2 and PTEN/STAT3 test whether the apparent modification is signature-B-specific or a more generic arbitrary-marker artifact.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 15 after H205-H216. Validation budget exhausted; no validation requested. Research_signature_B is now a key context issue. PTEN-loss/STAT3 association is robust in signature_B <=0.5 (H207/H209/H210), attenuated to near-zero in signature_B >=0.5 and >=1 (H205/H211), while direct high-B means H206/H208 are too small and not supported. Accept H205 active as within-dataset context attenuation, accept H211 closed as pre-registered extreme-high confirmation. CDKN2A-loss/MDM2 is strongly modified upward by high signature_B (H216 +0.195 [0.116,0.274], about 0.86 MDM2 SD); accept active but do not interpret causally because signature_B is constructed. Signature_B controls: SMARCA2 H212 null, USP7 H213 modest opposite attenuation not accepted, NFE2L2 H214 null, WRN H215 null; thus not generic modifier. Proposed next: direct MDM2 CDKN2A estimates in B>=0.5 and B<=0.5, MDM2 B>=1 interaction, MDM2 high-B within TP53-intact or low-9p21 strata, marker-D controls for MDM2 and PTEN/STAT3. Accepted headline within-dataset associations remain: TP53 non-loss stronger USP7, SMARCA4 loss stronger SMARCA2, MSI-high stronger WRN, KEAP1 loss weaker NFE2L2, PTEN loss stronger STAT3 overall, CDKN2A loss stronger MDM2 especially low 9p21 and now modified by signature_B. All are associations only, not causal or generalizable claims."
