  "narrative": "I assess the due validation response for H180. Under direction -1, positive signed estimates mean that exposed CDKN2A-loss cells have more negative MDM2 dependency scores, i.e. stronger MDM2 dependency. H180 tests CDKN2A loss versus CDKN2A intact among TP53-intact, MTAP-intact, low-9p21 cells. Discovery R155 gave a signed effect of +0.1126 [0.0578,0.1674] in 231 versus 98 cells, and independent validation R166 gave +0.0848 [0.0037,0.1659] in 245 versus 83 cells. The strict validation interval excludes zero and the point estimate is roughly 0.37 MDM2 SD and about 31% of the absolute mean MDM2 score, so the direction and practical magnitude are supported, although the lower validation bound is below the 10% relative benchmark because this nested stratum is small. I accept H180 as a supported within-dataset association and keep it closed; the precise magnitude in this sparse low-9p21 TP53/MTAP-intact stratum remains less certain than the broader CDKN2A-MDM2 association.\n\nFinal synthesis. Because dependency scores are negative-valued continuous quantities, I judged scientific meaningfulness primarily against outcome SDs and secondary relative-magnitude benchmarks. All claims are associations in the supplied dataset only. They are not causal statements, not claims that the measured predictor drives dependency, and not guaranteed to generalize beyond this cohort, lineage, culture, library, batch, or screen-quality distribution.\n\nThe strongest and most consistently validated associations are selective dependencies rather than broad population effects. First, TP53 non-loss is associated with stronger USP7 dependency: H6 gave validated +0.811 [0.782,0.841], about 2.2 USP7 SD, and the effect is reproduced across library, batch, culture, QC, aneuploidy, and other strata. Second, SMARCA4 loss is associated with stronger SMARCA2 dependency: H7 gave validated +0.805 [0.774,0.836], about 2.2 SMARCA2 SD, and the pattern is not explained by ARID1A loss. Third, MSI-high is associated with stronger WRN dependency: H9 gave validated +0.790 [0.736,0.843], about 3.0 WRN SD, and this is reproduced in TP53, library, batch, QC, mutation-burden, and BRCA2-restricted strata. Fourth, KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency: H13 gave validated +0.802 [0.775,0.829] in the registered positive direction, about 2.2 NFE2L2 SD. Fifth, PTEN loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency: H94 gave validated +0.292 [0.213,0.370], about 1.2 STAT3 SD, and this effect is STAT3-selective across many other dependency axes; batch-A stratum remains unresolved, but the main effect is robust. Sixth, CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger MDM2 dependency: overall H154 gave validated +0.114 [0.067,0.161]; TP53-intact cells H142 gave validated +0.159 [0.101,0.218]; low-9p21 cells H166 gave validated +0.110 [0.036,0.184]; and H180 now validates the low-9p21 TP53/MTAP-intact subgroup in the same direction. CDKN2A-MDM2 is not a broad dependency effect: CDKN2A loss is null for USP7, WRN, STAT3, SMARCA2, and NFE2L2, while MTAP-alone effects are weak or null and interaction tests do not strongly support MTAP dependence.\n\nThe negative findings are scientifically important because they reduce simple driver-gene matching and broad confounding explanations. KRAS mutation does not predict stronger KRAS dependency; BRAF V600E does not predict stronger BRAF dependency; EGFR amplification does not predict stronger EGFR dependency; ERBB2 amplification does not predict stronger ERBB2 dependency. TP53 loss is not associated with stronger MDM2 dependency in the primary test and is not a broad driver of STAT3, DHX9, KIF18A, SMARCA2, or WRN effects. PIK3CA, MYC amplification, STK11 loss, RB1 loss, BRCA2 loss, APC, SMAD4, NF1, and most constructed marker effects are null or unsupported as broad predictors. PTEN loss does not broadly predict EGFR, KIF18A, KRAS, USP7, SMARCA2, WRN, MDM2, TMED10, POLR2A, RPL11, NFE2L2, or BRAF dependency. These negative specificity tests make the accepted associations more selective.\n\nThe main unresolved layer is context dependence involving research_signature_b. For PTEN/STAT3, the accepted stronger PTEN-loss effect is preserved in low and middle signature-B strata: H207 +0.392 [0.327,0.457], H209 +0.367 [0.278,0.456], H210 +0.387 [0.256,0.517]. In high signature-B strata, direct mean differences H206 and H208 are near zero and not supported as meaningful direct positive differences, while interactions H205 +0.411 [0.333,0.488] and H211 +0.338 [0.254,0.422] support attenuation toward zero. I accept H205 and H211 as within-dataset context associations but keep H205 active because research_signature_b is an artificial constructed assay and no independent validation budget remains. Control interactions show that signature-B is not a generic modifier: SMARCA4/SMARCA2 H212, KEAP1/NFE2L2 H214, and MSI/WRN H215 are null; USP7/TP53 H213 is only a modest opposite-signed attenuation and is not promoted. The new strong signature-B result is H216: CDKN2A-loss MDM2 dependency is much stronger in high signature-B cells, interaction +0.195 [0.116,0.274], about 0.86 MDM2 SD. I accept H216 as a within-dataset discovery but keep it active because it is post-primary-discovery context modification, lacks external validation, and could be a constructed-assumption artifact unless direct stratum and marker-control analyses align.\n\nOther unresolved issues are more modest. PTEN-STAT3 batch-A stratum H99 remains unresolved because validation crossed zero. Sparse 9p21 subgroups such as H181, H183, H186, and some copy-number thresholds remain limited by small cells. Several screen-library and batch interaction tests remain deferred or unresolved because of sparse cells. The key next analysis should not seek new external validation, because the validation budget is exhausted; instead, it should convert the active signature-B interactions into direct stratum-specific estimates and arbitrary-marker controls. H217-H219 estimate CDKN2A-MDM2 effects directly in high, low, and extreme high signature-B; H220 and H221 test high-signature-B effects within TP53-intact and low-9p21 mechanistic contexts; H222 and H223 test marker-D interactions for MDM2/CDKN2A and STAT3/PTEN. I additionally registered high-signature-B direct estimates within TP53-loss MDM2/CDKN2A, MTAP-intact MDM2/CDKN2A, and PTEN/STAT3 split by TP53 status. If high signature-B direct CDKN2A-MDM2 effects remain large and marker-D controls are null, signature-B can be treated as a real within-dataset context modifier. If direct high-B effects are small or marker-D interactions mimic signature-B, the signature-B findings should remain non-headline artifacts of constructed assays. For PTEN/STAT3, the direct TP53-stratum high-B tests will show whether attenuation is broadly shared or TP53-dependent. Accepted headline conclusions remain unchanged: TP53 status/USP7, SMARCA4 loss/SMARCA2, MSI-high/WRN, KEAP1 loss/weak NFE2L2, PTEN loss/STAT3, and CDKN2A loss/MDM2, with the H180 low-9p21 TP53/MTAP-intact CDKN2A-MDM2 stratum now independently validated in direction.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 15 synthesis. Validation budget exhausted. Due H180 R166 assessed: CDKN2A-loss MDM2 effect in TP53-intact, MTAP-intact, low-9p21 validated in positive signed direction +0.0848 [0.0037,0.1659]; accept H180, closed. Overall CDKN2A-MDM2, TP53-intact CDKN2A-MDM2, and low-9p21 CDKN2A-MDM2 remain robust; H180 magnitude less certain in sparse stratum. Active unresolved layers: H205 PTEN-STAT3 signature-B attenuation accepted active, H216 CDKN2A-MDM2 signature-B upward modification accepted active. Need direct stratum conversions and arbitrary-marker controls. Active registered follow-ups H217-H223 remain relevant; new proposals add high-B TP53-loss CDKN2A-MDM2, high-B MTAP-intact CDKN2A-MDM2, high-B PTEN-STAT3 within TP53-intact and TP53-loss. Interpretation plan: if high-B CDKN2A-MDM2 direct effects large and marker-D null, keep signature-B context as supported within-dataset; if small or marker-D mimics, demote to artifact. Same logic for PTEN-STAT3 high-B attenuation. Accepted headline within-dataset associations: TP53 non-loss stronger USP7; SMARCA4 loss stronger SMARCA2; MSI-high stronger WRN; KEAP1 loss weaker NFE2L2; PTEN loss stronger STAT3; CDKN2A loss stronger MDM2, including validated low-9p21 TP53/MTAP-intact H180. Negative driver matching: KRAS/BRAF/EGFR/ERBB2 mutation or amplification not associated with matched dependency. Specificity negative findings support accepted effects but do not establish causality or generalizability."
