  "narrative": "No independent validation can be requested because the voluntary validation budget is exhausted. All estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For direction -1 mean differences, a positive signed estimate corresponds to a raw exposed-minus-comparator negative difference, i.e. more negative dependency scores in the exposed group and therefore stronger dependency. For direction -1 interactions, a positive signed estimate means the raw exposed-comparator effect is more negative/stronger in the named subgroup than in its complement. For direction +1 interactions, a positive signed estimate means the raw interaction is more positive relative to the complement, which for the accepted PTEN-loss/STAT3 pattern indicates attenuation toward zero.\n\nThe new direct stratum analyses strongly support the CDKN2A-loss/MDM2-dependency association inside high research_signature_b contexts. H217 gives a signed direct effect of +0.2497 [0.1794, 0.3200] in cells with research_signature_b >= 0.5, which is about 1.1 MDM2 SD and much larger than the nominal benchmark. I accept and close H217. H218 gives a smaller but statistically supported effect in research_signature_b <= 0.5, +0.0547 [0.0177, 0.0916], about 0.24 MDM2 SD. Its lower confidence bound is close to zero, but it is direction-consistent and plausibly above a 10% absolute-mean scale difference; I accept it as a modest direct effect and close it. H220 (+0.2491 [0.1721, 0.3262] within TP53-intact high-signature_b cells), H221 (+0.2745 [0.1886, 0.3604] within low copy_number_9p21 high-signature_b cells), and H225 (+0.2577 [0.1782, 0.3372] within MTAP-intact high-signature_b cells) are large, robust, and support the high-signature_b CDKN2A-MDM2 association without invoking TP53 loss, low 9p21 context, or MTAP status. I accept and close those direct robustness strata.\n\nThe specificity controls are mostly reassuring. H222 tests CDKN2A-loss/MDM2 interaction in research_marker_d-positive cells and is null: -0.0219 [-0.0912, 0.0475]. H234 tests the analogous marker-E interaction and is essentially null: -0.00046 [-0.0699, 0.0690]. H223 tests PTEN-loss/STAT3 interaction in marker-D-positive cells and is null: +0.0170 [-0.0877, 0.1218]. H232 and H233 test whether high-signature_b CDKN2A loss spuriously modifies USP7 or STAT3 dependencies; both are near null (+0.0040 [-0.0666, 0.0746] and -0.0211 [-0.0537, 0.0114], respectively). I reject these registered direction-specific interaction or direct-effect claims. They do not support arbitrary marker mimicry of the accepted CDKN2A-MDM2 and PTEN-STAT3 associations, and they support MDM2/STAT3 dependency-axis selectivity.\n\nThe main caution is that research_signature_b is not uniquely associated with context modification. H236 tests CDKN2A-loss/MDM2 interaction in research_signature_c >= 0.5 and is strongly positive under the registered direction: +0.3880 [0.2996, 0.4764], i.e. the CDKN2A-MDM2 effect is much stronger in signature_c-positive cells than in their complement. This is evidence that another constructed signature can mimic the signature_b context pattern. I accept H236 as a within-dataset association, but I keep it active and interpret it as a warning that the signature_b modification may be a constructed-assay/context artifact rather than a biologically specific modifier. H237 similarly tests PTEN-loss/STAT3 interaction in research_signature_a >= 0.5 and is strongly positive under its registered direction: +0.4892 [0.3855, 0.5930], indicating a strong context-dependent modification of the PTEN-loss/STAT3 association by another constructed signature. I accept H237 as a within-dataset association and keep it active, but do not promote it as biologically meaningful without validation. I registered direct stratum analyses for signature_c and signature_a to estimate raw high- and lower-signature effects, because interaction estimates alone cannot show whether the mimicking signature has a large raw exposed-comparator effect or mainly reflects a contrast with its complement. These direct tests will help determine whether the signature_c and signature_a findings are robust stratum effects or further evidence of arbitrary constructed-assay context modification. All accepted effects remain within-dataset associations, not causal claims or generalizable biological findings.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 16 appraise update. Validation budget exhausted; no validation requested. The direct CDKN2A-loss/MDM2 high-signature_b effect is strongly supported and robust across TP53-intact, low-9p21, and MTAP-intact strata: H217 +0.250, H220 +0.249, H221 +0.275, H225 +0.258, all direction -1 signed positive, meaning raw CDKN2A-loss cells have more negative MDM2 dependency and stronger MDM2 dependency. H218 low-signature_b direct effect is also positive but modest: +0.055. Marker-D and marker-E interaction controls for CDKN2A-MDM2 and PTEN-STAT3 are null, and CDKN2A-loss high-signature_b direct effects on USP7 and STAT3 are null, supporting dependency-axis selectivity and reducing broad arbitrary-marker mimicry.\n\nImportant competing explanation: H236 shows that research_signature_c also strongly modifies CDKN2A-MDM2 (+0.388 interaction), and H237 shows research_signature_a strongly modifies PTEN-STAT3 (+0.489 interaction under its registered direction). These are not biologically assigned assays. Therefore research_signature_b context effects should not be promoted as uniquely meaningful biological context; they are supported within-dataset assay/context associations, with signature_c and signature_a mimicry or additional context modification. I registered direct mean_difference tests for CDKN2A-MDM2 in high and low research_signature_c and for PTEN-STAT3 in high and low research_signature_a to estimate raw stratum effects and clarify whether the interaction patterns reflect large direct effects. Next analysis should prioritize untested robustness/mechanistic strata for research_signature_b (H219, H224, H226-H231, H235) plus the new direct signature_c/signature_a tests. Headline accepted within-dataset dependencies remain TP53 non-loss/USP7, SMARCA4 loss/SMARCA2, MSI-high/WRN, KEAP1 loss/weaker NFE2L2, PTEN loss/STAT3, and CDKN2A loss/MDM2. The signature context layer remains active and non-headline unless direct stratum tests and remaining controls make it more interpretable."
