  "narrative": "No independent validation can be requested because the voluntary validation budget is exhausted. All estimates below are already signed to the registered claim direction. For direction -1 direct MDM2 claims, a positive signed estimate means CDKN2A-loss cells have more negative MDM2 dependency scores, i.e. stronger dependency. For direction +1 NFE2L2 claims, a positive signed estimate means the accepted weaker-dependency direction for KEAP1 loss. For interactions, a positive signed estimate means the effect is amplified in the named subgroup relative to its complement under the registered direction.\n\nThe new direct strata strongly support the high-research_signature_c concentration of the CDKN2A-loss/MDM2-dependency association. H246 gives +0.385 [0.290, 0.480] in TP53-intact, high-signature-c cells; H247 gives +0.411 [0.198, 0.624] in TP53-loss, high-signature-c cells. The latter has a small exposed cell count, but the interval still clearly excludes zero, so the effect is robust enough to accept while noting imprecision. H248 gives +0.428 [0.312, 0.543] in high screen-ROC cells, H249 gives +0.415 [0.315, 0.515] in non-KY library cells, and H250 gives +0.406 [0.289, 0.523] in extreme signature-c cells. H256 gives +0.119 [0.052, 0.187] in batch A, consistent with the already validated overall CDKN2A-MDM2 effect. I therefore accept and close H246-H250 and H256. These are within-dataset robustness checks for the association, not evidence of causality or external generalizability.\n\nThe specificity controls mostly support selectivity of the high-signature-c modification for MDM2. H251, the interaction of TP53 loss and high signature_c for USP7 dependency, gives a small positive signed estimate +0.031 [-0.013, 0.075]; the interval includes zero, so the registered amplification claim is not supported. H252 for SMARCA4 loss/SMARCA2 gives +0.007 [-0.034, 0.048], essentially null. H254 for KEAP1 loss/NFE2L2 gives -0.010 [-0.050, 0.031], also null under the registered direction. H255 for MTAP loss as an overall predictor of MDM2 dependency gives only +0.019 [-0.008, 0.045]; this is small, statistically unresolved, and below the rough 10% absolute-mean benchmark for MDM2, so MTAP alone is not supported as a useful simple predictor. I reject and close H251, H252, H254, and H255.\n\nH253 is more informative than a simple null. For the PTEN-loss/STAT3 interaction with high research_signature_c, the signed estimate under the registered direction -1 is -0.163 [-0.270, -0.056]. Because this is negative when signed to direction -1, the raw interaction is opposite to the registered hypothesis: PTEN loss appears associated with less strong STAT3 dependency in high-signature-c cells relative to the complement. This magnitude is large relative to STAT3 dependency scale and exceeds the 10% benchmark, but it does not support H253 as registered. I therefore reject H253 in its original direction. I keep H253 active and register refinements: a reversed-direction interaction claim and direct PTEN-loss/STAT3 estimates in high versus low signature_c. These are exploratory refinements motivated by R221 and are needed to determine whether the attenuation is robust and whether the PTEN effect remains present but weaker in high signature_c.\n\nH257 tests a high research_signature_a threshold for PTEN loss/STAT3 dependency and gives a very large +0.627 [0.500, 0.755] signed estimate under direction -1. This strongly supports the already observed signature_a context modification of PTEN-STAT3, while again remaining an internal association rather than a causal mechanism.\n\nMultiplicity and causal interpretation are important. The CDKN2A-MDM2 signature-c strata are large, internally consistent across TP53 status, screen quality, library type, extreme signature-c, and batch A, which makes false-positive interpretation less plausible, but they still reflect constructed assay context rather than biological assignment. The null interactions for USP