{"proposals":[],"assessments":[{"claim":"H253","status":"reject","investigation":"closed","evidence":[]},{"claim":"H258","status":"accept","investigation":"closed"},{"claim":"H259","status":"unresolved","investigation":"active"},{"claim":"H260","status":"unresolved","investigation":"active"}],"narrative":"No new validation was released, assessments_due is empty, and the independent validation budget is exhausted, so synthesis is based on the accumulated discovery and prior validation evidence. The headline dataset-supported dependency associations are large, internally coherent, and mostly independently validated. TP53 non-loss versus TP53 loss is associated with much stronger USP7 dependency, with validated signed effect +0.811 [0.782, 0.841]; equivalently TP53 loss is associated with markedly weaker USP7 dependency. SMARCA4 loss versus non-loss is associated with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency, validated +0.805 [0.774, 0.836]. MSI-high versus MSS is associated with much stronger WRN dependency, validated +0.790 [0.736, 0.843]. KEAP1 loss versus non-loss is associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency; after direction correction the validated estimate is +0.802 [0.775, 0.829]. PTEN loss versus non-loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency, validated overall +0.292 [0.213, 0.370] and strong in the TP53-loss stratum +0.442 [0.265, 0.619]. CDKN2A loss versus non-loss is associated with stronger MDM2 dependency, validated overall +0.114 [0.067, 0.161], TP53-intact +0.159 [0.101, 0.218], and low copy_number_9p21 +0.110 [0.036, 0.184]. These effects are large on the dependency-score scale and well above the practical 10 percent clinical-significance benchmark. Some highly conditioned CDKN2A-MDM2 strata are smaller and less certain, for example the TP53-intact/MTAP-intact/low-9p21 validated effect +0.085 [0.004, 0.166] has a lower bound near zero, so it should not be promoted as a uniformly large conditional effect.

The context-assay findings are internal associations rather than biological mechanisms. High research_signature_c sharply concentrates the CDKN2A-loss/MDM2 association: accepted direct estimates are +0.385 [0.290, 0.480] in TP53-intact, +0.411 [0.198, 0.624] in TP53-loss, +0.428 [0.312, 0.543] in high screen-quality cells, +0.415 [0.315, 0.515] in non-KY library cells, +0.406 [0.289, 0.523] in extreme signature-c cells, and +0.119 [0.052, 0.187] in batch A. This pattern is internally robust, but it reflects a constructed assay context and does not establish causality or external generalizability. High research_signature_a also amplifies PTEN-loss/STAT3 dependency, with an extreme high-signature-a estimate +0.627 [0.500, 0.755]. I now reassess the signature-c PTEN-STAT3 interaction. H253 remains rejected as originally registered because the signed discovery estimate is -0.163 [-0.270, -0.056], meaning the raw interaction is opposite to the anticipated amplification. The reversed claim H258 is accepted because the same evidence signed to the reverse direction is +0.163 [0.056, 0.270], indicating that PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency is meaningfully attenuated in high research_signature_c relative to its complement. This is an important within-dataset context finding, but direct high-versus-low signature_c PTEN-STAT3 strata are still needed to quantify whether the attenuated high-signature-c association remains substantial.

Important negative or null findings bound the conclusions. KRAS mutation does not predict KRAS dependency, BRAF V600E does not predict BRAF dependency, EGFR amplification does not predict EGFR dependency, and ERBB2 amplification does not predict ERBB2 dependency. TP53 loss is not a simple MDM2-dependency driver in the reciprocal direction; MTAP loss is weak or null after conditioning on CDKN2A, and simple MTAP-alone MDM2 dependency is not supported. CDKN2A loss does not spill over onto USP7, STAT3, WRN, SMARCA2, or NFE2L2. PTEN loss is selective for STAT3 and does not predict MDM2, USP7, SMARCA2, WRN, EGFR, KIF18A, POLR2A, RPL11, or TMED10 dependency in the broad tests. Constructed markers D/E/F and many technical strata mostly provide negative controls or unresolved low-count contexts; they do not add general biological roles. Unresolved uncertainty remains mainly in low-count technical or lineage strata, batch-A PTEN-STAT3 validation, the small lower bound of one conditioned CDKN2A-MDM2 stratum, and direct high-versus-low research_signature_c PTEN-STAT3 estimates. If further analysis is allowed, the most informative next step is to analyze H259 and H260, the direct PTEN-loss/STAT3 mean differences inside high and low research_signature_c strata, because they will show whether attenuation by signature-c is a residual but reduced PTEN effect or a near-null effect. Secondary controls such as marker-F and APC negative tests can be retained only if capacity remains.","research_notes":"Iteration 18 synthesis complete. Validation budget is exhausted; no validation requested. Assessment update: H253 original rejected and closed; H258 reversed signature-c PTEN-STAT3 attenuation accepted from discovery evidence. H259 and H260 remain active and are the highest-priority next discovery analyses. Final accepted headline axes: TP53 non-loss stronger USP7, SMARCA4-loss stronger SMARCA2, MSI-high stronger WRN, KEAP1-loss weaker NFE2L2, PTEN-loss stronger STAT3, CDKN2A-loss stronger MDM2. Context associations: high research_signature_c concentrates CDKN2A-MDM2; high research_signature_a amplifies PTEN-STAT3; high research_signature_c attenuates PTEN-STAT3; apparent signature-b MDM2 effect is largely explained after signature-c conditioning. These are within-dataset associations, not causal biology or external generalizable effects. Do not pursue more signature-context axes unless H259/H260 justify them; otherwise final report can stand with unresolved low-count technical/context controls."}

