  "narrative": "All estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For the direction -1 STAT3 and MDM2 claims, a positive signed estimate means the exposed genetic or loss state is associated with a more negative dependency score, i.e. stronger dependency. For the direction +1 NFE2L2 claims, a positive signed estimate means the accepted weaker NFE2L2 dependency direction for KEAP1 loss. Validation requests are unavailable because the voluntary validation budget is exhausted, so these are discovery-evidence assessments only and do not establish external generalizability.  The new direct research_signature_c strata clarify the PTEN-loss STAT3 context effect. H259 gives +0.156 with 95% interval [0.071, 0.242] in high research_signature_c cells, while H260 gives +0.319 with [0.255, 0.384] in low research_signature_c cells. This supports the previously accepted reversed interaction interpretation: PTEN loss remains associated with stronger STAT3 dependency in high signature_c cells, but the effect is substantially attenuated relative to low signature_c. The point estimate is above the 10% practical benchmark, although the lower confidence bound is below 10%, so the residual high-signature-c effect is statistically robust and moderate but less certain as a clinically significant effect. I therefore accept H259 and H260 and close them.  The four research_signature_c by research_signature_a cells make the PTEN STAT3 context structure more specific. H261, high signature_c and low signature_a, gives only +0.060 [-0.020, 0.140], which is small and statistically unresolved, so I reject and close H261 as a meaningful stronger-dependency claim. H262, high signature_c and high signature_a, gives +0.469 [0.253, 0.685], a large effect despite the minimum exposed cell count of 20; I accept H262 with caution about small-cell precision. H263, low signature_c and high signature_a, gives +0.648 [0.548, 0.749], a very strong effect, and H264, low signature_c and low signature_a, gives +0.144 [0.080, 0.209], a moderate effect whose point estimate exceeds 10% although the lower bound is below 10%. The pattern supports a context interaction rather than a uniform signature_c modifier: high signature_a is strongly associated with a large PTEN-loss STAT3 effect even when signature_c is high, whereas low signature_a in high signature_c yields a weak or null effect. This is within-dataset context modification, not causal biology.  The new MDM2 crossed cells sharpen specificity. H266 gives +0.334 [0.230, 0.437] for CDKN2A loss when signature_c is high and signature_a is low, while H265 gives -0.010 [-0.057, 0.038] when signature_a is high and signature_c is low. The latter is effectively null and the point estimate is in the opposite signed direction, so I reject H265 and close it. H266 supports signature_c-specific concentration of the CDKN2A-loss MDM2 association, not broad high-signature context modification by signature_a. To complete the 2x2, I register a new low-signature_c and low-signature_a MDM2 stratum as a refinement motivated by R233 and R232.  The KEAP1 loss NFE2L2 direct strata are very large and consistent. H37 in TP53-loss cells gives +0.810 [0.763, 0.857], and H38 in TP53-intact cells gives +0.792 [0.770, 0.815]. Both strongly support the accepted weaker NFE2L2 dependency direction and are compatible with the earlier null TP53 interaction test. I accept and close H37 and H38. The adenocarcinoma lineage strata also support robust internal reproducibility: H32 gives +0.799 [0.776, 0.823] for TP53 non-loss versus loss for USP7 dependency, and H34 gives +0.777 [0.755, 0.799] for SMARCA4 loss for SMARCA2 dependency. I accept and close both. Overall, the new evidence strengthens the core dependency associations and refines the constructed-signature context findings: PTEN STAT3 is amplified by signature_a and attenuated by signature_c; CDKN2A MDM2 is concentrated primarily by signature_c; KEAP1 NFE2L2, TP53 USP7, SMARCA4 SMARCA2, and MSI WRN remain robust.",
