  "narrative": "No new validation was released and no response-deadline assessments are pending, and the voluntary independent validation budget is exhausted. I close the three remaining untested formal interaction proposals H305-H307 as unresolved rather than leaving them active, because the analysis and validation budgets are not available to address them and further unstructured threshold stratification has low expected value. This synthesis is based on the accepted discovery claims in the supplied dataset plus previously returned within-study validation comparisons. For direction -1 dependency-score claims, a positive signed estimate means the exposed predictor is associated with a more negative, stronger CRISPR dependency score. For the accepted NFE2L2/KEAP1 claims in the direction +1 reversed framework, a positive signed estimate encodes less negative NFE2L2 dependency, i.e. weaker dependency after KEAP1 loss. I use about 0.10 absolute dependency-score units as a conservative practical meaningfulness benchmark because the outcomes are centered negative CRISPR scores and a relative 10 percent rule is not directly interpretable on this scale. SUPPORTED FINDINGS. Four very large measured dependency axes are robust in this dataset. First, TP53 non-loss is associated with much stronger USP7 dependency than TP53 loss, discovery estimate about +0.802 [0.782,0.822] and independent validation estimate about +0.811 [0.782,0.841]; this remains very large across adenocarcinoma, adherent culture, library strata, batch A, screen-quality strata, aneuploidy strata, MYC-amplified cells, KEAP1-loss cells, high EMT context, high research_signature_a, low research_signature_a, low serum, and other accepted contexts. Second, SMARCA4 loss is associated with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency than SMARCA4 non-loss, discovery estimate about +0.784 [0.765,0.803] and validation estimate about +0.805 [0.774,0.836]; this synthetic-lethality-like association is retained across ARID1A-loss strata, ARID1A-non-loss strata, lineage, culture, screen quality, batch A, library strata, STK11-loss cells, high stemness, higher ploidy, high research_signature_a, and low research_signature_a. The corresponding ARID1A, TP53, lineage, signature_b, signature_c, and marker interaction tests do not support additional effect modification. Third, MSI-high is associated with much stronger WRN dependency than non-MSI-high, discovery estimate about +0.790 [0.760,0.819] and validation estimate about +0.790 [0.736,0.843]; this is retained across mutation-burden thresholds, TP53 strata, lineage, library, culture, screen quality, BRCA2-loss exclusion, high hypoxia, research_signature_a strata, and direct high/low signature contexts, though some exposed cells are small. Fourth, KEAP1 loss is associated with much less negative NFE2L2 scores, i.e. weaker NFE2L2 dependency in the accepted reversed direction, with discovery estimate about +0.796 [0.776,0.816] and validation estimate about +0.802 [0.775,0.829]; this association persists across TP53 strata, lineage, STK11-loss cells, library, culture, batch A, screen quality, high IFN-gamma context, and research_signature_a strata. Two moderate axes are also supported. PTEN loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency, overall discovery estimate about +0.267 [0.215,0.319] and validation estimate about +0.292 [0.213,0.370]. It is accepted in TP53-intact cells about +0.287 [0.227,0.347], and in TP53-loss cells about +0.190 [0.085,0.296] with validation about +0.442 [0.265,0.619]. It is accepted across high and low hypoxia direct strata, about +0.250 [0.149,0.352] and +0.288 [0.213,0.362], across screen-quality strata, culture, lineage, kras strata, pik3ca strata, and many constructed-signature contexts. Its magnitude is strongly context-modified: high research_signature_a direct estimate about +0.604 [0.513,0.695], high research_signature_a interaction estimate about +0.489 [0.385,0.593], high research_signature_a with low research_signature_c about +0.648 [0.548,0.749], and high research_signature_a with high research_signature_c about +0.469 [0.253,0.685], whereas high research_signature_b direct estimate about +0.018 [-0.025,0.061] is rejected; low research_signature_b direct estimate about +0.392 [0.327,0.457] and the corresponding reversed interaction about +0.411 [0.333,0.488] are accepted. High research_signature_c direct estimate about +0.156 [0.071,0.242] is accepted but smaller, and high research_signature_c with low research_signature_a about +0.060 [-0.020,0.140] is rejected as not robustly meaningful. Thus PTEN-STAT3 is most clearly expressed in high research_signature_a and lower research_signature_b/research_signature_c contexts, but these signature labels are constructed assays and not assigned biological pathways. CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger MDM2 dependency, overall discovery estimate about +0.117 [0.082,0.152] and validation estimate about +0.114 [0.067,0.161]. It is accepted in TP53-intact cells about +0.118 [0.079,0.158] with validation about +0.159 [0.101,0.218], in 9p21-low cells about +0.135 [0.091,0.179] with validation about +0.110 [0.036,0.184], in TP53-loss 9p21-low cells about +0.204 [0.106,0.303], in TP53-loss/MTAP-non-loss cells about +0.100 [0.018,0.181], and in high research_signature_c contexts about +0.390 [0.304,0.475], with the high signature_c interaction about +0.388 [0.300,0.476]. The strongest signature-cell estimates are high research_signature_b with high research_signature_c about +0.765 [0.692,0.838] and high signature_c with low signature_a about +0.334 [0.230,0.437]. By contrast, high research_signature_a with low research_signature_c is null about -0.010 [-0.057,0.038], low signature_c low signature_a is null about +0.007 [-0.019,0.032], and direct low research_signature_a about +0.096 [0.057,0.134] falls just below the practical benchmark and is not accepted as independently meaningful. Direct high and low MYC-RNA strata are similar, about +0.111 [0.060,0.163] and +0.104 [0.047,0.161], supporting a broadly retained CDKN2A-MDM2 association rather than a clear MYC-expression modification; however, the formal MYC interaction H306 was not tested and is now closed. NEGATIVE OR BOUNDED FINDINGS. Driver-matched dependency effects are not supported in this dataset: KRAS mutation does not predict KRAS dependency, BRAF V600E does not predict BRAF dependency, EGFR amplification does not predict EGFR dependency, and ERBB2 amplification does not predict ERBB2 dependency; EGFR amplification also did not predict KRAS or TMED10 dependency in broad tests. The originally registered TP53-loss MDM2 direction is rejected, and MTAP loss does not provide a robust independent MDM2 signal after conditioning on CDKN2A. PTEN loss is selective for STAT3 among the tested dependency axes; it is rejected for MDM2, USP7, SMARCA2, WRN, EGFR, KIF18A, POLR2A, RPL11, TMED10, BRAF, and most specificity tests, with DHX9 and RIT1 tests under high screen quality also rejected as small or imprecise. CDKN2A loss is selective for MDM2 and is rejected as spilling over to USP7, STAT3, WRN, SMARCA2, or NFE2L2 dependency. Research markers D, E, and F behave largely as low-information or negative-control strata, and research signatures are constructed standardized assays without assigned gene or pathway meaning. Some nominally detected small effects, such as TP53 loss for KIF18A about +0.021 [0.001,0.040] and RB1 loss for POLR2A about +0.025 [-0.001,0.051], are rejected as not practically meaningful. Many formal interaction tests for lineage, TP53, ARID1A, MTAP, batch, library, markers, MYC amplification, and other technical or biological contexts are rejected or unresolved, generally because intervals are wide, cells are small, or effects are too small for the dependency scale. Screen-quality eligibility may be collider-like because screen performance can depend on cell state and genotype, so high-quality-screen nulls are bounded evidence rather than proof of absence. UNRESOLVED UNCERTAINTY. The batch-A PTEN-loss STAT3 subgroup remains unresolved because validation estimate about +0.159 [-0.018,0.335] crosses zero despite positive discovery. Several signature and TP53-stratum decompositions involve small exposed cells, especially high research_signature contexts and some high-hypoxia MSI-high WRN cells. The formal hypoxia interaction H305, MYC-RNA interaction H306, and STK11-loss SMARCA4-SMARCA2 interaction H307 remain untested and are closed. Deferred technical interactions, such as library and batch modifications, also remain unresolved. All validation here is internal to the supplied lung-cell-line CRISPR screen dataset and should not be interpreted as external replication, causality, or clinical generalizability. MULTIP LICITY is another limitation: many subgroup and signature tests were performed, so the strongest accepted patterns should be regarded as internally consistent measured associations that would benefit from pre-specified external confirmation. MOST INFORMATIVE NEXT ANALYSIS. Further within-dataset threshold stratification is unlikely to change the main conclusions. The highest-value next step is adequately powered, pre-specified external validation of the two context-sensitive moderate axes: PTEN-loss STAT3 in high research_signature_a and lower research_signature_b/c contexts, and CDKN2A-loss MDM2 in high research_signature_c and TP53-intact or 9p21-low contexts. A targeted validation design should pre-specify these interaction hypotheses rather than perform additional exploratory thresholds. To move from association to mechanism or therapeutic relevance, experimental perturbation of TP53, USP7, SMARCA4/SMARCA2, MSI/WRN biology, KEAP1/NFE2L2 signaling, PTEN/STAT3, and CDKN2A/9p21/MDM2 biology would be needed. The four very large dependency axes and the two moderate axes are the main scientifically meaningful findings supported by this dataset."
}

