  "narrative": "This final discovery batch quantifies the direct PTEN-loss STAT3 association in high versus lower IFN-gamma strata, tests whether IFN-gamma modifies the CDKN2A-loss MDM2 association, tests IFN-gamma specificity for the four largest dependency axes, and completes PTEN-loss specificity for DHX9 and RIT1. I used the same conservative audit rule: for these centered continuous dependency scores, an association is treated as practically and inferentially supportable when the signed estimate is materially substantial, generally at least about 0.10 absolute dependency-score units, the 95% interval excludes zero, and the pattern is directionally coherent with the registered hypothesis and related context analyses. A raw 10% relative rule is difficult on this negative-centered dependency-score scale, so I used an approximately 0.10 absolute practical floor together with uncertainty and consistency. Direction convention remains important: for direction -1 claims, positive signed estimates mean the exposed group has a more negative dependency score, i.e. stronger dependency; for direction -1 interactions, positive signed interaction means the exposed-minus-comparator contrast is more negative in the named subgroup than in its complement. For the accepted reversed KEAP1-NFE2L2 axis, direction +1 means positive estimates encode less negative NFE2L2 scores after KEAP1 loss, i.e. weaker measured dependency. H325 gives +0.428 [0.326, 0.529] in high IFN-gamma cells and H326 gives +0.207 [0.148, 0.266] in lower/equal IFN-gamma cells; both are large, exclude zero, and support a genuine PTEN-loss association with stronger STAT3 dependency in both IFN strata. The high-minus-lower difference is roughly 0.221, which coheres with the accepted H320 IFN-gamma interaction +0.221 [0.104, 0.338]. H328 +0.439 [0.326, 0.553] and H329 +0.227 [0.158, 0.295] within TP53-intact cells show that this context effect is not driven only by TP53-loss cells; PTEN-loss cells in high IFN-gamma 