efore: very large robust USP7, SMARCA2, WRN, and reversed NFE2L2 associations; moderate PTEN-STAT3 association with accepted IFN-gamma context dependence; moderate CDKN2A-MDM2 association without IFN-gamma-specific support; and no support for IFN-gamma modification of the large axes or for PTEN loss altering DHX9 or RIT1.",
  "research_notes": "Final within-dataset analysis status. The accepted large axes remain: TP53 non-loss versus loss with much stronger USP7 dependency, SMARCA4 loss with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency, MSI-high with much stronger WRN dependency, and KEAP1 loss with weaker measured NFE2L2 dependency operationalized as less negative scores. These are internally robust, often validated, and not meaningfully modified by IFN-gamma according to H332-H335. The moderate PTEN-loss STAT3 association is robust overall and is now internally quantified across IFN contexts: high IFN PTEN-loss contrast +0.428 [0.326, 0.529] (H325/R300) and lower/equal IFN +0.207 [0.148, 0.266] (H326/R301), with the formal interaction accepted in H320 +0.221 [0.104, 0.338] (R290). TP53-intact replication is strong: high IFN +0.439 [0.326, 0.553] (H328/R303) and lower IFN +0.227 [0.158, 0.295] (H329/R304). Therefore PTEN-STAT3 is context sensitive but not exclusive to IFN-gamma; the effect is present in both strata and stronger in high IFN context. The IFN context is not causal and may reflect measured biology, collinearity, or selection effects. The moderate CDKN2A-loss MDM2 association remains supported overall, with context modification mainly supported by 9p21-low and signature-C-containing contexts, not by IFN-gamma. H327 formal IFN interaction for CDKN2A-MDM2 is -0.060 [-0.150, 0.030], and H330 direct TP53-intact high IFN estimate is +0.050 [-0.036, 0.137]; both rejected as unsupported context-specific claims, with uncertainty remaining. PTEN-loss specificity is now broadly completed: PTEN loss supports STAT3 but is rejected or small for DHX9, RIT1, MDM2, USP7, SMARCA2, WRN, EGFR, KIF18A, POLR2A, RPL11, TMED10, and BRAF. Driver-matched dependency associations for KRAS, BRAF, EGFR, and ERBB2 remain unsupported. Technical and biological modifiers largely do not materially alter the large axes, though some nested signature contexts involving signature C and PTEN STAT3 remain context-rich and require external validation. H320 is closed because direct high/lower IFN estimates have been delivered, but external pre-specified validation remains the best next step for PTEN-STAT3 IFN contexts and CDKN2A-MDM2 signature/9p21 contexts. All claims are associations in the supplied lung-cell-line CRISPR dependency dataset, not causal claims, therapeutic claims, or generalizable biological facts."
